            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">13</span></span>
          end for
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">14</span></span>
          end for
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.18" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;"># Phase II: Continuous pre-training </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">15</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.4.19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for<span id="algorithm1.4.19.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <em id="algorithm1.4.19.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">each pre-training epoch</em> </span>do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.20" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">16</span></span>
          Sample pairs <math id="algorithm1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{q}_{i},e_{i})\in\mathcal{Q}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{q}_{i},e_{i})\in\mathcal{Q}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> from each domain <math id="algorithm1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.21" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.21.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">17</span></span>
          Compute domain prototype <math id="algorithm1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.22" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.22.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">18</span></span>
          Compute prototype contrastive loss: <math id="algorithm1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{proto}}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>proto</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{proto}}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Eq. (<a href="#S4.E7" title="In 4.1. Generalized GFM as Cross-domain Retriever ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>);
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.23" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.23.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">19</span></span>
          Compute information gain contrast <math id="algorithm1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{IGC}}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>IGC</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{IGC}}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Eq. (<a href="#S4.E8" title="In 4.1. Generalized GFM as Cross-domain Retriever ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>);
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.24" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.24.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">20</span></span>
          <math id="algorithm1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{Phase II}}=\alpha_{2}\mathcal{L}_{\text{proto}}+\alpha_{3}\mathcal{L}_{\text{IGC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>Phase II</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>proto</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>IGC</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{Phase II}}=\alpha_{2}\mathcal{L}_{\text{proto}}+\alpha_{3}\mathcal{L}_{\text{IGC}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#S4.E9" title="In 4.1. Generalized GFM as Cross-domain Retriever ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>)).;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.25" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.25.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">21</span></span>
          end for
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.26" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1. </span>Computational Complexity of the Pre-training Stage</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The pre-training stage consists of two phases:
<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1)</span> mixed-domain KG completion pre-training (Phase I), and
<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2)</span> prototype-driven continuous pre-training (Phase II).
Unless otherwise stated, we focus on the asymptotic complexity with respect to graph size, and omit constant factors related to embedding dimensionality and the internal implementations of neural modules (<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{Msg}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Msg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{Msg}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{Update}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Update</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{Update}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{Agg}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Agg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{Agg}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{MLP}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">MLP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{MLP}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">etc.</span>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase I: Mixed-domain KG Completion Pre-training.</span>
Phase I performs KG completion over the multi-domain indexed graph <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}=(\mathcal{V},\mathcal{R},\mathcal{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=(\mathcal{V},\mathcal{R},\mathcal{E})</annotation></semantics></math> using query-conditioned GFM inference. For each masked triple, a pseudo-query <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math> is constructed.</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Embedding initialization.</span>
Initializing entity and relation embeddings for all <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> requires <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{R}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{R}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Query-conditioned message passing.</span>
For each GFM layer, messages are computed over all edges <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,r,v)\in\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,r,v)\in\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> and aggregated at each node. The per-layer complexity is <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{V}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{V}|)</annotation></semantics></math>, and stacking <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> layers yields <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(L(|\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{V}|))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(L(|\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{V}|))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Entity relevance scoring.</span>
Computing <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\mathbf{q}}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\mathbf{q}}(e)</annotation></semantics></math> for all entities requires a forward pass of an MLP, which requires <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KG completion loss.</span>
Both <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{BCE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>BCE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{BCE}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{rank}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>rank</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{rank}}</annotation></semantics></math> involve summations over positive and negative entity sets whose union equals <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, their computation costs <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Summing up, time complexity for Phase I is <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(L|\mathcal{E}|+L|\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{R}|+|\mathcal{V}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(L|\mathcal{E}|+L|\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{R}|+|\mathcal{V}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{E}|\geqslant|\mathcal{V}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{E}|\geqslant|\mathcal{V}|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, it can be simplified to <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(L|\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{R}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(L|\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{R}|)</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(L|\mathcal{E}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(L|\mathcal{E}|)</annotation></semantics></math> being the dominant term.
If masking over all triples in <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> once per epoch, the per-epoch complexity becomes:</p>
<table id="A2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\big(L|\mathcal{E}|^{2}+|\mathcal{E}||\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{E}||\mathcal{R}|\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\big(L|\mathcal{E}|^{2}+|\mathcal{E}||\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{E}||\mathcal{R}|\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">which is dominated by <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(L|\mathcal{E}|^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(L|\mathcal{E}|^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase II: Prototype-driven Continuous Pre-training.</span>
Phase II performs semantic alignment using a subset of query-entity pairs <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{d\in\mathcal{D}}\mathcal{Q}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{d\in\mathcal{D}}\mathcal{Q}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> sampled from each domain.</p>
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prototype construction.</span>
Computing domain prototypes needs averaging entity representations, yielding <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\sum_{d\in\mathcal{D}}|\mathcal{Q}_{d}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\sum_{d\in\mathcal{D}}|\mathcal{Q}_{d}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prototype contrastive loss.</span>
For each pair, the softmax denominator sums over all domains, yielding <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}((\sum_{d\in\mathcal{D}}|\mathcal{Q}_{d}|)\cdot|\mathcal{D}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}((\sum_{d\in\mathcal{D}}|\mathcal{Q}_{d}|)\cdot|\mathcal{D}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Information gain contrast regularization.</span>
The KL-divergence is calculated over the entity distribution <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\mathbf{q}}(e)\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{V}|\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\mathbf{q}}(e)\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{V}|\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each query, this requires <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)</annotation></semantics></math> time, yielding <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}((\sum_{d\in\mathcal{D}}|\mathcal{Q}_{d}|)\cdot|\mathcal{V}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}((\sum_{d\in\mathcal{D}}|\mathcal{Q}_{d}|)\cdot|\mathcal{V}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GFM forward inference.</span>
Since <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\mathbf{q}}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\mathbf{q}}(e)</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the query-conditioned GFM output, each query requires an <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-layer message-passing forward pass, incurring <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(L(|\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{V}|))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(L(|\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{V}|))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Over all sampled queries, this contributes <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}((\sum_{d\in\mathcal{D}}|\mathcal{Q}_{d}|)\cdot L|\mathcal{E}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}((\sum_{d\in\mathcal{D}}|\mathcal{Q}_{d}|)\cdot L|\mathcal{E}|)</annotation></semantics></math>,
which is the dominant cost in Phase II.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Combining all, the per-epoch complexity of Phase II is:</p>
<table id="A2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\Big(\big(\sum_{d\in\mathcal{D}}|\mathcal{Q}_{d}|\big)\cdot(L|\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{D}|)\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\Big(\big(\sum_{d\in\mathcal{D}}|\mathcal{Q}_{d}|\big)\cdot(L|\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{D}|)\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overall Pre-training Complexity.</span>
Combining Phase I and Phase II, the total per-epoch time complexity of pre-training is:</p>
<table id="A2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\big(L|\mathcal{E}|^{2}+|\mathcal{E}||\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{E}||\mathcal{R}|\big)+\mathcal{O}\Big(\sum_{d\in\mathcal{D}}|\mathcal{Q}_{d}|(L|\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{D}|)\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\big(L|\mathcal{E}|^{2}+|\mathcal{E}||\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{E}||\mathcal{R}|\big)+\mathcal{O}\Big(\sum_{d\in\mathcal{D}}|\mathcal{Q}_{d}|(L|\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{D}|)\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Since Phase II is performed on a subset and Phase I dominates in large-scale knowledge graphs, the overall complexity is asymptotically governed by <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(L|\mathcal{E}|^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(L|\mathcal{E}|^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, which highlights that the computational cost of pre-training is primarily determined by repeated query-conditioned message passing over the entire indexed graph, which motivates our later use of parameter-efficient fine-tuning and subgraph-level optimization in the downstream stages.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span>Fine-tuning with the Subgraph Selector.</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm2.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>
The multi-domain indexed KG <math id="algorithm2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}=(\mathcal{V},\mathcal{R},\mathcal{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=(\mathcal{V},\mathcal{R},\mathcal{E})</annotation></semantics></math>;
frozen entity embeddings <math id="algorithm2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{e}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{e}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="algorithm2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>; training queries <math id="algorithm2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\mathbf{q},\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}^{+})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\mathbf{q},\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}^{+})\}</annotation></semantics></math>;
hyper-parameters <math id="algorithm2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>Trained subgraph selector producing <math id="algorithm2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm2.4.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.3.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">each mini-batch <math id="algorithm2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> of queries</em> <span id="algorithm2.4.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm2.4.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.4.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">each query <math id="algorithm2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}\in\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}\in\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm2.4.4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
            Construct query prompt <math id="algorithm2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}=\operatorname{MLP}(\mathbf{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>MLP</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}=\operatorname{MLP}(\mathbf{q})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm2.4.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.6.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">each entity <math id="algorithm2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm2.4.6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">Learn query-conditioned subgraph </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.8.1" class="ltx_text"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm2.4.8.3" class="ltx_text">Query-conditioned entity: <math id="algorithm2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{Z}}_{e}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{Z}}_{e}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Eq. (<a href="#S4.E10" title="In 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>);</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
            Sample selection gate: <math id="algorithm2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{e}(\mathbf{q})\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{e}(\mathbf{q})\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Eq. (<a href="#S4.E11" title="In 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>);
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
            end for
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></span>
            Induce subgraph <math id="algorithm2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> by thresholding <math id="algorithm2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">Label-free IB regularization </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.13.1" class="ltx_text"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">9</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm2.4.13.3" class="ltx_text">Retrieval loss: <math id="algorithm2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{BCE}}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>BCE</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{BCE}}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Eq. (<a href="#S4.E5" title="In 4.1. Generalized GFM as Cross-domain Retriever ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), <math id="algorithm2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{rank}}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>rank</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{rank}}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Eq. (<a href="#S4.E6" title="In 4.1. Generalized GFM as Cross-domain Retriever ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>);</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10</span></span>
            Pooled subgraph representation: <math id="algorithm2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}}=\sum_{e\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}}S_{e}(\mathbf{q})\cdot\widetilde{\mathbf{Z}}_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}}=\sum_{e\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}}S_{e}(\mathbf{q})\cdot\widetilde{\mathbf{Z}}_{e}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">11</span></span>
            Lower bound of <math id="algorithm2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="algorithm2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{NCE}}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>NCE</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{NCE}}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Eq. (<a href="#S4.E15" title="In Proposition 4.3 (Lower Bound of 𝐼(q,𝒢_q)). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>);
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.16" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">12</span></span>
            Penalties: <math id="algorithm2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{size}}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>size</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{size}}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Eq. (<a href="#S4.E16" title="In Proposition 4.4 (Upper Bound of 𝐼(𝒢,𝒢_q)). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), <math id="algorithm2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{con}}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>con</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{con}}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Eq. (<a href="#S4.E16" title="In Proposition 4.4 (Upper Bound of 𝐼(𝒢,𝒢_q)). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>);
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.17" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">13</span></span>
            Combine the IB surrogate: <math id="algorithm2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil\mathcal{L}_{\text{LIB}}\rceil\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>LIB</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil\mathcal{L}_{\text{LIB}}\rceil\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Eq. (<a href="#S4.E19" title="In 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>);
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.18" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">14</span></span>
            Calculate the final fine-tuning loss: <math id="algorithm2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{ftn}}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ftn</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{ftn}}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Eq. (<a href="#S4.E18" title="In 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>);
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.19" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">15</span></span>
            end for
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.20" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">16</span></span>
            Update selector parameters via gradient descent;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.21.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">17</span></span>
            end for
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.22" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2. </span>Computational Complexity of the Fine-tuning Stage</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The fine-tuning stage optimizes the label-free IB objective (Eq. (<a href="#S4.E13" title="In 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>)) via tractable surrogate using Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 4.3 (Lower Bound of 𝐼(q,𝒢_q)). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> (Eq. (<a href="#S4.E15" title="In Proposition 4.3 (Lower Bound of 𝐼(q,𝒢_q)). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>)) and Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Proposition 4.4 (Upper Bound of 𝐼(𝒢,𝒢_q)). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a> (Eq. (<a href="#S4.E17" title="In Proposition 4.4 (Upper Bound of 𝐼(𝒢,𝒢_q)). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>)), together with supervised retrieval loss (Eq. (<a href="#S4.E5" title="In 4.1. Generalized GFM as Cross-domain Retriever ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#S4.E6" title="In 4.1. Generalized GFM as Cross-domain Retriever ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)).
Follow the same protocal in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1. Computational Complexity of the Pre-training Stage ‣ Appendix B Algorithm and Complexity Analysis ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, we omit constant factors related to hidden dimensions and the internal implementations of neural modules (<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{MLP}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>MLP</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{MLP}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>), focusing on asymptotic dependence on graph and batch sizes.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Per-query Complexity (mini-batch <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span>
For a query <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, the fine-tuning stage consists of the following computation modules.</p>
<ul id="A2.I3" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Query prompt construction.</span>
Prompt <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}=\operatorname{MLP}(\mathbf{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>MLP</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}=\operatorname{MLP}(\mathbf{q})</annotation></semantics></math> is computed once per query.
Treating <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{MLP}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>MLP</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{MLP}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> as a constant-cost operator <span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">w.r.t.</span> graph size, this step requires <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Query-conditioned entity embedding construction.</span>
For every entity <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, we form <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{Z}}_{e}=\big[\mathbf{Z}_{e}^{\star}\ \|\ \mathbf{W}_{1}\mathbf{p}\ \|\ \mathbf{W}_{2}\mathbf{q}\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐩</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{Z}}_{e}=\big[\mathbf{Z}_{e}^{\star}\ \|\ \mathbf{W}_{1}\mathbf{p}\ \|\ \mathbf{W}_{2}\mathbf{q}\big]</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a per-entity operation. Thus, the complexity is <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Differentiable subgraph gate sampling.</span>
For each <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Gumbel-Sigmoid gate <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{e}(\mathbf{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{e}(\mathbf{q})</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E11" title="In 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) is computed once. This is also linear in the number of entities: <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Subgraph induction by thresholding.</span>
Constructing <math id="A2.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> requires one pass over all entities that yields <math id="A2.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Subgraph generation.</span> Inducing <math id="A2.I3.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I3.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.I3.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be done by scanning edges, which is at most <math id="A2.I3.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}|)</annotation></semantics></math>. We state explicitly below as an optional dominant term if full edge scanning is used.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Supervised retrieval loss.</span>
Both <math id="A2.I3.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{BCE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>BCE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{BCE}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I3.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{rank}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>rank</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{rank}}</annotation></semantics></math> sum over positives <math id="A2.I3.i6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and negatives <math id="A2.I3.i6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In the worst case, they are computed over all entities and yield <math id="A2.I3.i6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)</annotation></semantics></math>, which matches the dependence of Eq. (<a href="#S4.E5" title="In 4.1. Generalized GFM as Cross-domain Retriever ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#S4.E6" title="In 4.1. Generalized GFM as Cross-domain Retriever ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) on entity-level distributions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pooled subgraph representation.</span>
The pooled <math id="A2.I3.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> requires iterating over the selected entity set <math id="A2.I3.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A2.I3.i7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}|)\leqslant\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}|)\leqslant\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Noise-contrastive estimation term.</span>
Eq. (<a href="#S4.E15" title="In Proposition 4.3 (Lower Bound of 𝐼(q,𝒢_q)). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) computes a denominator summing over negative pairs <math id="A2.I3.i8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}},\mathbf{q}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}},\mathbf{q}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.I3.i8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assuming <math id="A2.I3.i8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is precomputed for all <math id="A2.I3.i8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> (as in Algorithm <a href="#algorithm2" title="In B.1. Computational Complexity of the Pre-training Stage ‣ Appendix B Algorithm and Complexity Analysis ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), computing the softmax-normalized score per query costs <math id="A2.I3.i8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{B}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{B}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.
(If <math id="A2.I3.i8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is not cached, the cost would inherit <math id="A2.I3.i8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}}|)</annotation></semantics></math> construction, which is accounted for by the pooled representation.)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Size penalty.</span>
The size term <math id="A2.I3.i9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{size}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>size</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{size}}</annotation></semantics></math> costs <math id="A2.I3.i9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}|)\leqslant\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}|)\leqslant\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i10" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Connectivity penalty.</span>
The connectivity term <math id="A2.I3.i10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{con}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>con</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{con}}</annotation></semantics></math> involves multiplication by the normalized Laplacian <math id="A2.I3.i10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Computing <math id="A2.I3.i10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{L}\mathbf{S}_{e}(\mathbf{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐋𝐒</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{L}\mathbf{S}_{e}(\mathbf{q})</annotation></semantics></math> can be implemented as the sparse matrix-vector multiplication with sparsity pattern given by <math id="A2.I3.i10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, which costs <math id="A2.I3.i10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}|)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is typically the dominant term among the regularizers.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Per-batch Complexity.</span>
Summing up, a single query <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math> gives:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)}_{\text{Eq.~{(\ref{eq:query_e})}}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)}_{\text{Eq.~{(\ref{eq:prob})}}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)}_{\text{thresholding}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{BCE}}\text{,}~\mathcal{L}_{\text{rank}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>Eq. (</mtext><mtext><a href="#S4.E10" title="In 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>Eq. (</mtext><mtext><a href="#S4.E11" title="In 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>thresholding</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>BCE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>,</mtext><mo lspace="0.270em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>rank</mtext></msub></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)}_{\text{Eq.~{(\ref{eq:query_e})}}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)}_{\text{Eq.~{(\ref{eq:prob})}}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)}_{\text{thresholding}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|)}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{BCE}}\text{,}~\mathcal{L}_{\text{rank}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\underbrace{\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}|)}_{\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\text{,}~\mathcal{L}_{\text{size}}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{B}|)}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{NCE}}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}|)}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{con}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>,</mtext><mo lspace="0.270em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>size</mtext></msub></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>NCE</mtext></msub></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>con</mtext></msub></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\underbrace{\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}|)}_{\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\text{,}~\mathcal{L}_{\text{size}}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{B}|)}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{NCE}}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}|)}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{con}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Using <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}|\leqslant|\mathcal{V}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}|\leqslant|\mathcal{V}|</annotation></semantics></math> and grouping terms, we obtain <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{B}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{B}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For a mini-batch <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, the total cost is <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{B}|\cdot(|\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{B}|))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{B}|\cdot(|\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{B}|))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Expanding the product yields <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{B}||\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{B}||\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{B}|^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{B}||\mathcal{V}|+|\mathcal{B}||\mathcal{E}|+|\mathcal{B}|^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
In typical large KGs, <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{E}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{E}|</annotation></semantics></math> dominates <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{B}|\ll|\mathcal{E}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{B}|\ll|\mathcal{E}|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, the fine-tuning is asymptotically dominated by the connectivity regularizer, giving <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{B}||\mathcal{E}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{B}||\mathcal{E}|)</annotation></semantics></math>, where the per-query dominant cost is <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Notably, if <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> are explicitly induced by scanning the full edge set each iteration, that additional cost is at most <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}|)</annotation></semantics></math> per query and is already subsumed by the <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}|)</annotation></semantics></math> term above.
In contrast, if one uses edge-indexing restricted to the selected node set <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the practical runtime can be reduced, but the worst-case asymptotic bound remains unchanged.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3. </span>Computational Complexity of the Inference Stage (QA)</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a query <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math> on the target knowledge graph <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}^{T}=(\mathcal{V}^{T},\mathcal{R}^{T},\mathcal{E}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}^{T}=(\mathcal{V}^{T},\mathcal{R}^{T},\mathcal{E}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math>, the inference stage consists of
<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1)</span> subgraph retrieval via the trained selector (Eq. (<a href="#S4.E11" title="In 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>)), and
<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2)</span> relational paths induced in-context prompting, including entity-to-document mapping and truncated DFS path extraction.
We omit constant factors related to hidden dimensions and neural module internals.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step-wise Complexity Analysis.</span>
For a single query <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, Algorithm <a href="#algorithm3" title="In B.3. Computational Complexity of the Inference Stage (QA) ‣ Appendix B Algorithm and Complexity Analysis ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> includes the following modules.</p>
<ul id="A2.I4" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Selection probability.</span>
The selector computes <math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{e}(\mathbf{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{e}(\mathbf{q})</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#S4.E11" title="In 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>)), which requires one pass over all entities, hence <math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(|\mathcal{V}^{T}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(|\mathcal{V}^{T}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Subgraph induction by thresholding.</span>
Constructing <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> costs <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}^{T}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}^{T}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> is explicitly induced from <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> by scanning all edges in <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, the worst-case additional cost is <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}^{T}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}^{T}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Entity weighting.</span>
For each entity <math id="A2.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math>, inference computes <math id="A2.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#S4.E20" title="In 4.3. Relation Paths Induced In-context Prompter ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>)), which is linear in the size of the selected entity set: <math id="A2.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.
(The term <math id="A2.I4.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{c}\mathbf{M}[e,c]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{c}\mathbf{M}[e,c]</annotation></semantics></math> can be precomputed per entity from the fixed mapping matrix <math id="A2.I4.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐌</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Document relevance computation.</span>
The document scores are given by <math id="A2.I4.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{c}=\mathbf{M}^{\top}w_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{c}=\mathbf{M}^{\top}w_{e}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Treating <math id="A2.I4.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}\in\{0,1\}^{|\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{q}}|\times|\mathcal{C}_{\mathbf{q}}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}\in\{0,1\}^{|\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{q}}|\times|\mathcal{C}_{\mathbf{q}}|}</annotation></semantics></math> as a sparse matrix, computing <math id="A2.I4.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}^{\top}w_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}^{\top}w_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sparse matrix-vector multiplication.
Its time complexity is proportional to the number of non-zeros (<math id="A2.I4.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{nnz}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>nnz</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{nnz}</annotation></semantics></math>) in <math id="A2.I4.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐌</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> restricted to the selected entities as <math id="A2.I4.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\mathrm{nnz}(\mathbf{M}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>nnz</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\mathrm{nnz}(\mathbf{M}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}}))</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.I4.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the submatrix induced by <math id="A2.I4.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In the worst case, this is upper-bounded by scanning all entity-to-chunk links in the query-restricted support, <span id="A2.I4.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, <math id="A2.I4.i4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{q}}||\mathcal{C}_{\mathbf{q}}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{q}}||\mathcal{C}_{\mathbf{q}}|)</annotation></semantics></math>,
while in practice it is typically much smaller due to sparsity.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Top-<math id="A2.I4.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> document selection.</span>
Selecting the top-<math id="A2.I4.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> documents from <math id="A2.I4.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{R_{c}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{R_{c}\}</annotation></semantics></math> can be done in <math id="A2.I4.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{C}_{\mathbf{q}}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{C}_{\mathbf{q}}|)</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="A2.I4.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, linear-time selection),
or <math id="A2.I4.i5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{C}_{\mathbf{q}}|\log|\mathcal{C}_{\mathbf{q}}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{C}_{\mathbf{q}}|\log|\mathcal{C}_{\mathbf{q}}|)</annotation></semantics></math> if full sorting is used.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Relational path extraction.</span>
In the worst case, enumerating all paths (<math id="A2.I4.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leqslant l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leqslant l</annotation></semantics></math>) may grow exponentially due to branching in DFS.
Denoting the maximum degree in the induced subgraph <math id="A2.I4.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A2.I4.i6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, the worst-case number of DFS expansions is <math id="A2.I4.i6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\Delta^{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\Delta^{l})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Path scoring.</span>
For each extracted path <math id="A2.I4.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, inference computes <math id="A2.I4.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{r}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{r}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#S4.E21" title="In 4.3. Relation Paths Induced In-context Prompter ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>)), which costs <math id="A2.I4.i7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(k)\leqslant\mathcal{O}(l)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(k)\leqslant\mathcal{O}(l)</annotation></semantics></math> per path, hence over all extracted paths requires <math id="A2.I4.i7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|\cdot l)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|\cdot l)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Path ranking and subset selecting.</span>
Ranking paths by <math id="A2.I4.i8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S_{r}(\pi)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S_{r}(\pi)\}</annotation></semantics></math> costs <math id="A2.I4.i8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|\log|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|\log|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|)</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="A2.I4.i8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|)</annotation></semantics></math> with top-<math id="A2.I4.i8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> selection.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLM answer generation.</span>
The answer generation <math id="A2.I4.i9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}=\operatorname{LLM}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>LLM</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}=\operatorname{LLM}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the LLM inference cost and prompt length. We omit it for brevity.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm3" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span>Inference with In-context Prompting.</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm3.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm3.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm3.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>
Query <math id="algorithm3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math>; target KG <math id="algorithm3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>;
trained selector producing <math id="algorithm3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{e}(\mathbf{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{e}(\mathbf{q})</annotation></semantics></math>;
entity-to-document mapping matrix <math id="algorithm3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐌</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}</annotation></semantics></math>;
DFS search hop limit <math id="algorithm3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>; top-<math id="algorithm3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> documents <math id="algorithm3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\mathbf{q}}^{(K)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>𝐪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\mathbf{q}}^{(K)}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm3.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>Generated answer <math id="algorithm3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// </span><span id="algorithm3.4.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">Subgraph retrieval </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm3.4.4.2" class="ltx_text">Selection probabilities <math id="algorithm3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{e}(\mathbf{q})\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{e}(\mathbf{q})\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Eq. (<a href="#S4.E11" title="In 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) for all <math id="algorithm3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\mathcal{V}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\mathcal{V}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
            Induce subgraph <math id="algorithm3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}=(\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}},\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{q}},\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}=(\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}},\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{q}},\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// </span><span id="algorithm3.4.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">Entity-to-document scoring </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm3.4.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for<span id="algorithm3.4.7.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <em id="algorithm3.4.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">each entity <math id="algorithm3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math></em> </span>do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
            Compute importance weight <math id="algorithm3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{e}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{e}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Eq. (<a href="#S4.E20" title="In 4.3. Relation Paths Induced In-context Prompter ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>);
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
            end for
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
            Compute relevance <math id="algorithm3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{c}=\mathbf{M}^{\top}w_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{c}=\mathbf{M}^{\top}w_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> and select top-<math id="algorithm3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> documents;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// </span><span id="algorithm3.4.11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">Reasoning path extraction. </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm3.4.12.2" class="ltx_text">Extract relational paths <math id="algorithm3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="algorithm3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> via <math id="algorithm3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-hop truncated DFS;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm3.4.13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm3.4.13.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">each path <math id="algorithm3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm3.4.13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">9</span></span>
            Compute path score <math id="algorithm3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{r}(\pi)\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{r}(\pi)\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Eq. (<a href="#S4.E21" title="In 4.3. Relation Paths Induced In-context Prompter ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>).

</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10</span></span>
            end for
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">11</span></span>
            Select top-ranked paths <math id="algorithm3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.17" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// </span><span id="algorithm3.4.17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">In-context prompting and generation </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">12</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm3.4.18.2" class="ltx_text">Construct prompt from <math id="algorithm3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and retrieved documents;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">13</span></span>
            Generate answer <math id="algorithm3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}=\operatorname{LLM}(\mathbf{q},\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}^{\star},\mathcal{C}_{\mathbf{q}}^{(K)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>LLM</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>𝐪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}=\operatorname{LLM}(\mathbf{q},\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}^{\star},\mathcal{C}_{\mathbf{q}}^{(K)})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.20" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overall Inference Complexity.</span>
Excluding the LLM generation cost, the per-query inference complexity is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}^{T}|)+\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\underbrace{\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}^{T}|)}_{\text{(optional, if inducing $\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{q}}$ by edge scan)}}\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!+\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}|)+\mathcal{O}\big(\mathrm{nnz}(\mathbf{M}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mpadded style="width:0em;" width="0em"><mo>+</mo></mpadded><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>(optional, if inducing </mtext><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">ℰ</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝐪</mi></msub><mtext> by edge scan)</mtext></mrow></munder><mpadded style="width:0em;" width="0em"><mo>+</mo></mpadded><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mpadded style="width:0em;" width="0em"><mo>+</mo></mpadded><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>nnz</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}^{T}|)+\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\underbrace{\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{E}^{T}|)}_{\text{(optional, if inducing $\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{q}}$ by edge scan)}}\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!+\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}|)+\mathcal{O}\big(\mathrm{nnz}(\mathbf{M}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}})\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{C}_{\mathbf{q}}|)+\mathcal{O}(\Delta^{l})+\mathcal{O}(|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|\cdot l)+\mathcal{O}(|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|\log|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>log</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{C}_{\mathbf{q}}|)+\mathcal{O}(\Delta^{l})+\mathcal{O}(|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|\cdot l)+\mathcal{O}(|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|\log|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}|\leqslant|\mathcal{V}^{T}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}|\leqslant|\mathcal{V}^{T}|</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the simplified bound:</p>
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\Big(|\mathcal{V}^{T}|+|\mathcal{E}^{T}|+\mathrm{nnz}(\mathbf{M}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}})+\Delta^{l}+|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|\log|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>nnz</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\Big(|\mathcal{V}^{T}|+|\mathcal{E}^{T}|+\mathrm{nnz}(\mathbf{M}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}})+\Delta^{l}+|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|\log|\Pi_{\mathbf{q}}|\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">In typical settings, the dominant cost is the truncated DFS path extraction, which can be exponential in the hop budget <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> in the worst case.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1. </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 4.1 (Multi-domain logical expressivity of query-conditioned GFM). ‣ 4.1. Generalized GFM as Cross-domain Retriever ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first restate Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 4.1 (Multi-domain logical expressivity of query-conditioned GFM). ‣ 4.1. Generalized GFM as Cross-domain Retriever ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> for reference.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="157.31" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 157.31" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,157.31) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 152.68 C 0 155.24 2.07 157.31 4.63 157.31 L 472.75 157.31 C 475.3 157.31 477.38 155.24 477.38 152.68 L 477.38 4.63 C 477.38 2.07 475.3 0 472.75 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 152.68 C 0.69 154.86 2.45 156.62 4.63 156.62 L 472.75 156.62 C 474.92 156.62 476.68 154.86 476.68 152.68 L 476.68 4.63 C 476.68 2.45 474.92 0.69 472.75 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.32 108.41)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.73em;--ltx-fo-height:3.15em;--ltx-fo-depth:7.45em;font-size:10pt;" height="146.67" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 43.59)" width="466.73"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.73em;">
<span id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 4.1 (Multi-domain logical expressivity of query-conditioned GFM). ‣ 4.1. Generalized GFM as Cross-domain Retriever ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a><span id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> (</span><span id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multi-domain logical expressivity of query-conditioned GFM</span><span id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">)
<span id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> be a knowledge graph indexed from multiple domains. <math id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(e)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Dom</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(e)\}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes unary predicates indicate domain attributes of entity <math id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math>. For a query <math id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, the query-conditioned GFM can learn a rule <math id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textnormal{{R}}(\textnormal{$\mathbf{q}$},e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathcolor="#000000">R</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textnormal{{R}}(\textnormal{$\mathbf{q}$},e)</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textnormal{{R}}(\textnormal{$\mathbf{q}$},e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathcolor="#000000">R</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textnormal{{R}}(\textnormal{$\mathbf{q}$},e)</annotation></semantics></math> is a formula in graded modal logic over <math id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> with constant <math id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists^{\geqslant N}e^{\prime}(\textnormal{{R}}(e^{\prime},e)\wedge\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(e^{\prime})\wedge\psi(e^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∃</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⩾</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathcolor="#000000">R</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∧</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Dom</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∧</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists^{\geqslant N}e^{\prime}(\textnormal{{R}}(e^{\prime},e)\wedge\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(e^{\prime})\wedge\psi(e^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS1.p2.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> a subformula.</span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}=(\mathcal{V},\mathcal{R},\mathcal{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=(\mathcal{V},\mathcal{R},\mathcal{E})</annotation></semantics></math> be the KG indexed from the multi-domain documents. <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}:\mathcal{V}\to\{0,1\}^{|\mathbb{D}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}:\mathcal{V}\to\{0,1\}^{|\mathbb{D}|}</annotation></semantics></math> maps each entity node to its domain attributes. We denote the unary predicate <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Dom</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> as true if the <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-th entry of <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> is 1. We assume the query-conditioned GFM <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{\theta}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{\theta}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> follows the message passing scheme defined in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E2" title="In 4.1. Generalized GFM as Cross-domain Retriever ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#S4.E3" title="In 4.1. Generalized GFM as Cross-domain Retriever ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).
To prove Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 4.1 (Multi-domain logical expressivity of query-conditioned GFM). ‣ 4.1. Generalized GFM as Cross-domain Retriever ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, we establish the equivalence between the logical formulas learnable by this GFM and the Graded Modal Logic (CML) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib78" title="" class="ltx_ref">De Rijke, 2000</a>; <a href="#bib.bib79" title="" class="ltx_ref">Otto, 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib77" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qiu et al., 2024</a>)</cite> extended with domain predicates.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1) Sufficiency (Constructive Proof).<span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
We prove that for any formula <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> in the multi-domain CML logic, there exists a parameterization of the GFM that learns <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>. We proceed by structural induction on the formula construction. The bad case is the atomic formulas (</span></span><span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span><span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text">, <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Dom</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(e)</annotation></semantics></math>) are directly contained in the initial entity embeddings <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{e}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{e}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>. A simple linear projection (1-layer GFM) can encode these embeddings, so that the base predicates are learnable.
For the inductive step, assume a sub-formula <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(e^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(e^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is learnable by a GFM with <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l-1</annotation></semantics></math> layers, such that the dimension <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{e^{\prime}}^{(l-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{e^{\prime}}^{(l-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> acts as an indication <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{e^{\prime}}^{(l-1)}[j]=\mathbb{I}(\mathcal{G},e^{\prime}\models\psi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊧</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{e^{\prime}}^{(l-1)}[j]=\mathbb{I}(\mathcal{G},e^{\prime}\models\psi)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the indicator.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We next show the formula <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(e)=\exists^{\geqslant N}e^{\prime}(\textnormal{{R}}(e^{\prime},e)\wedge\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(e^{\prime})\wedge\psi(e^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩾</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">R</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Dom</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(e)=\exists^{\geqslant N}e^{\prime}(\textnormal{{R}}(e^{\prime},e)\wedge\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(e^{\prime})\wedge\psi(e^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math> is learnable by the <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer.
The semantics of <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(e)</annotation></semantics></math> require counting neighbors <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> connected by relation <span id="A3.SS1.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">R</span> that satisfy both the domain constraint <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Dom</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> and the property <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>. We construct the <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer aggregation following Lemma C.3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib77" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qiu et al., 2024</a>)</cite>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Message Construction.<span id="A3.SS1.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Let the message function <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{Msg}_{\textnormal{{R}}}^{(l)}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Msg</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">R</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{Msg}_{\textnormal{{R}}}^{(l)}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> select and combine the relevant features. Since <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(e^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Dom</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(e^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is a unary predicate available in the input features (and preserved or propagated to <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(l-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(l-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer), let <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{e^{\prime}}^{(l-1)}[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{e^{\prime}}^{(l-1)}[k]</annotation></semantics></math> correspond to <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(e^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Dom</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(e^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. We define the message to output a scalar value 1 only if both conditions are met, essentially implementing a logical “AND” (<math id="A3.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\wedge" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\wedge</annotation></semantics></math>) via soft continuous approximation (</span></span><span id="A3.SS1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span><span id="A3.SS1.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text">, using summing components or MLP approximation in the limit):</span></p>
<table id="A3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}_{e^{\prime},e}\doteq\mathbb{I}\big(\mathbf{Z}_{e^{\prime}}^{(l-1)}[k]=1\wedge\mathbf{Z}_{e^{\prime}}^{(l-1)}[j]=1\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>∧</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}_{e^{\prime},e}\doteq\mathbb{I}\big(\mathbf{Z}_{e^{\prime}}^{(l-1)}[k]=1\wedge\mathbf{Z}_{e^{\prime}}^{(l-1)}[j]=1\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Alternatively, in a standard linear GNN, <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{\textsc{Msg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Msg</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{\textsc{Msg}}</annotation></semantics></math> assigns a unit weight to the <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> dimension conditioned on <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> being masked or filtered by domain <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. A more robust construction uses the universal approximation theorem of MLPs (contained in <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{Msg}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Msg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{Msg}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>) to map <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{e^{\prime}}^{(l-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{e^{\prime}}^{(l-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> to 1 if the domain and <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> bits are active, and 0 otherwise.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Aggregation.<span id="A3.SS1.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
The GFM sums the messages from neighbors:</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{e}=\sum_{e^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}_{\textnormal{{R}}}(e)}\mathbf{m}_{e^{\prime},e}=\left|\{e^{\prime}\mid\textnormal{{R}}(e^{\prime},e)\wedge\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(e^{\prime})\wedge\psi(e^{\prime})\}\right|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">R</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">R</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Dom</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{e}=\sum_{e^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}_{\textnormal{{R}}}(e)}\mathbf{m}_{e^{\prime},e}=\left|\{e^{\prime}\mid\textnormal{{R}}(e^{\prime},e)\wedge\operatorname{Dom}_{d}(e^{\prime})\wedge\psi(e^{\prime})\}\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">This sum <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> exactly counts the number of valid logical witnesses in the specific domain.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Thresholding (Quantifier Realization).<span id="A3.SS1.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
To realize the quantifier <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists^{\geqslant N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mo>∃</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩾</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists^{\geqslant N}</annotation></semantics></math>, we set the bias term <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math> and use a step-like activation function <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> (</span></span><span id="A3.SS1.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span><span id="A3.SS1.p8.1.3" class="ltx_text">, a steep Sigmoid). Assume <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}=-N+\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}=-N+\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, then:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{e}^{(l)}=\sigma(S_{e}-N+\delta),\quad\delta&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{e}^{(l)}=\sigma(S_{e}-N+\delta),\quad\delta&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{e}\geqslant N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>⩾</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{e}\geqslant N</annotation></semantics></math>, the input to <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is positive, outputting 1 (True). If <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{e}&lt;N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{e}&lt;N</annotation></semantics></math>, the output is 0 (False).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the GFM can structurally implement the formula <math id="A3.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(e)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2) Necessity (Expressivity Limit).<span id="A3.SS1.p10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Deriving from Theorem C.2 and Theorem C.7 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib77" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qiu et al. (2024)</a></cite>, we prove any rule learnable by the query-conditioned GFM corresponds to a CML formula over <math id="A3.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>. We invoke the established correspondence between MPNNs and the 1-dimensional Weisfeiler-Leman (1-WL) test <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib75" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. It is known that the discriminative power of standard MPNNs is bounded by 1-WL. Furthermore, the stable coloring of 1-WL on a graph is equivalent to the logical equivalence classes defined by CML with counting quantifiers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib80" title="" class="ltx_ref">Barceló et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib81" title="" class="ltx_ref">Morris et al., 2019</a>)</cite>. In our specific case:</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Graph Augmentation.<span id="A3.SS1.p11.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
The multi-domain graph <math id="A3.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> can be viewed as a standard colored graph where the initial node colors <math id="A3.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(v)</annotation></semantics></math> are tuples <math id="A3.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{I}(v=\textnormal{$\mathbf{q}$}),\operatorname{Dom}_{d_{1}}(v),\cdots,\operatorname{Dom}_{d_{k}}(v),\cdots)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐪</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Dom</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Dom</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{I}(v=\textnormal{$\mathbf{q}$}),\operatorname{Dom}_{d_{1}}(v),\cdots,\operatorname{Dom}_{d_{k}}(v),\cdots)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bisimulation Invariance.<span id="A3.SS1.p12.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
GFM is permutation invariant. If two entities <math id="A3.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> are indistinguishable by CML formulas (</span></span><span id="A3.SS1.p12.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span><span id="A3.SS1.p12.1.3" class="ltx_text">, bisimilar on the augmented graph), they will receive identical message aggregates at every step and thus identical final embeddings.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">In conclusion, if the GFM learns a classifier that distinguishes entity <math id="A3.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> based on <math id="A3.SS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textnormal{{R}}(\textnormal{$\mathbf{q}$},e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">R</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textnormal{{R}}(\textnormal{$\mathbf{q}$},e)</annotation></semantics></math>, there must exist a distinguishing structure in the computation tree. Since the computation tree is isomorphic to the unrolled logic formula in CML, the decision boundary learned by the GFM must be describable by a CML formula.
Specifically, the “multi-domain” property simply expands the set of atomic unary predicates in the logic. If a rule relies on checking <math id="A3.SS1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Dom}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Dom</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Dom}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, this is valid in CML as checking an atomic proposition. If the rule cannot be expressed in CML (</span><span id="A3.SS1.p13.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span><span id="A3.SS1.p13.1.3" class="ltx_text">, it requires counting cycles or checking connectivity beyond tree-unrolling), the 1-WL test would fail to distinguish the relevant subgraphs, and the GFM would consequently fail to learn the rule.
Therefore, a rule is learnable only if it is expressible in CML with domain predicates.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2. </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title='Proposition 4.2 (Error Bound of ℒ_"LIB" Approximation). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first restate Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title='Proposition 4.2 (Error Bound of ℒ_"LIB" Approximation). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> for reference.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="108" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 108" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,108) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 103.37 C 0 105.93 2.07 108 4.63 108 L 472.75 108 C 475.3 108 477.38 105.93 477.38 103.37 L 477.38 4.63 C 477.38 2.07 475.3 0 472.75 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 103.37 C 0.69 105.55 2.45 107.31 4.63 107.31 L 472.75 107.31 C 474.92 107.31 476.68 105.55 476.68 103.37 L 476.68 4.63 C 476.68 2.45 474.92 0.69 472.75 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.32 59.09)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.73em;--ltx-fo-height:3.15em;--ltx-fo-depth:3.89em;font-size:10pt;" height="97.36" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 43.59)" width="466.73"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.73em;">
<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title='Proposition 4.2 (Error Bound of ℒ_"LIB" Approximation). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a><span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> (</span><span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Error Bound of <math id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{LIB}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">LIB</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{LIB}}</annotation></semantics></math> Approximation</span><span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">)
<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the subgraph, <math id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> the ground-truth answer, and <math id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math> the query. Assume the Markov property <math id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle y\leftrightarrow\mathbf{q}\leftrightarrow\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">↔</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">↔</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle y\leftrightarrow\mathbf{q}\leftrightarrow\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> exists, the approximation error of <math id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{IB}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">IB</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{IB}}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{LIB}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">LIB</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{LIB}}</annotation></semantics></math> is upper-bounded by the conditional entropy of <math id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|I(y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})-I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\right|\leqslant H(\mathbf{q}\mid y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⩽</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|I(y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})-I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\right|\leqslant H(\mathbf{q}\mid y),</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\mathbf{q}\mid y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\mathbf{q}\mid y)</annotation></semantics></math> is a data-dependent constant.<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We formally analyze the approximation error introduced by the label-free objective using the interaction information and the chain rule of mutual information. Let the random variables <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the ground-truth answer, the query, and the retrieved subgraph, respectively.
Consider the joint mutual information <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(y,\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(y,\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math>. By symmetry, we can decompose this term in two equivalent ways based on the chain rule:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(y,\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})=I(y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})+I(\mathbf{q}\mid y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(y,\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})=I(y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})+I(\mathbf{q}\mid y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(y,\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})=I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})+I(y\mid\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(y,\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})=I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})+I(y\mid\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Subtracting Eq. (<a href="#A3.E5" title="In Proof. ‣ C.2. Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>) from Eq. (<a href="#A3.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ C.2. Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>) allows us to isolate the discrepancy between the supervised objective <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math> and our proposed label-free proxy <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})-I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})=I(y\mid\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})-I(\mathbf{q}\mid y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})-I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})=I(y\mid\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})-I(\mathbf{q}\mid y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">To derive an upper bound, we recall the property that mutual information is bounded by the entropy of its variables. Specifically, for conditional mutual information, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X;Y\mid Z)=H(X\mid Z)-H(X\mid Y,Z)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X;Y\mid Z)=H(X\mid Z)-H(X\mid Y,Z).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since entropy is non-negative and conditioning reduces entropy, or leaves it unchanged, we know that:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X;Y\mid Z)\leqslant H(Y\mid Z)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X;Y\mid Z)\leqslant H(Y\mid Z),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Shannon entropy. Applying this inequality to both terms on the RHS of Eq. (<a href="#A3.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ C.2. Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(y\mid\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\leqslant H(y\mid\mathbf{q})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(y\mid\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\leqslant H(y\mid\mathbf{q}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\mathbf{q}\mid y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\leqslant H(\mathbf{q}\mid y)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\mathbf{q}\mid y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\leqslant H(\mathbf{q}\mid y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting these bounds back into the absolute difference error:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|I(y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})-I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|I(y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})-I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\max\big(H(y\mid\mathbf{q})+H(\mathbf{q}\mid y)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\max\big(H(y\mid\mathbf{q})+H(\mathbf{q}\mid y)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant H(y\mid\mathbf{q})+H(\mathbf{q}\mid y)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant H(y\mid\mathbf{q})+H(\mathbf{q}\mid y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">In the context of retrieval where the query intends to specify the answer (</span><span id="A3.SS2.p3.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span><span id="A3.SS2.p3.7.3" class="ltx_text">, <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math> is not independent of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>), if we assume the retrieved subgraph <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> only contains information about <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> via the semantics of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math> (Markov property <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle y\!\leftrightarrow\!\mathbf{q}\!\leftrightarrow\!\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">↔</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">↔</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle y\!\leftrightarrow\!\mathbf{q}\!\leftrightarrow\!\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>), the bound tightens to:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|I(y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})-I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\right|\leqslant H(\mathbf{q}\mid y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|I(y;\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})-I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\right|\leqslant H(\mathbf{q}\mid y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text">While <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\mathbf{q}\mid y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\mathbf{q}\mid y)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the intrinsic diversity of queries targeting the same answer, it is crucial to note that this term is determined solely by the data distribution <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{q},y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{q},y)</annotation></semantics></math> and remains constant with respect to the learnable parameters in the subgraph selector. Therefore, minimizing the upper bound is equivalent to minimizing the proxy gap up to a constant additive factor. The gradient directions for optimizing sufficiency are essentially unaffected by this term.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">In conclusion, Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title='Proposition 4.2 (Error Bound of ℒ_"LIB" Approximation). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> suggests maximizing the mutual information with query <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}};\mathbf{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}};\mathbf{q})</annotation></semantics></math> is an effective proxy for <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}};y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}};y)</annotation></semantics></math>, provided that the query ambiguity <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(y\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(y\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math> is low. Since the query is designed to point towards the answer (low ambiguity), minimizing the label-free loss effectively minimizes the supervised loss within a controllable error margin.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3. </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 4.3 (Lower Bound of 𝐼(q,𝒢_q)). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first restate Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 4.3 (Lower Bound of 𝐼(q,𝒢_q)). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> for reference.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="159.63" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 159.63" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,159.63) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 155 C 0 157.56 2.07 159.63 4.63 159.63 L 472.75 159.63 C 475.3 159.63 477.38 157.56 477.38 155 L 477.38 4.63 C 477.38 2.07 475.3 0 472.75 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 155 C 0.69 157.18 2.45 158.94 4.63 158.94 L 472.75 158.94 C 474.92 158.94 476.68 157.18 476.68 155 L 476.68 4.63 C 476.68 2.45 474.92 0.69 472.75 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.32 110.72)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.73em;--ltx-fo-height:3.15em;--ltx-fo-depth:7.62em;font-size:10pt;" height="148.99" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 43.59)" width="466.73"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.73em;">
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 4.3 (Lower Bound of 𝐼(q,𝒢_q)). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a><span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> (</span><span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lower Bound of <math id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">q</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">)
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Denote the average-pooled subgraph representation as <math id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}}=\sum_{e\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}}S_{e}(\mathbf{q})\cdot\widetilde{\mathbf{Z}}_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐆</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}}=\sum_{e\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{q}}}S_{e}(\mathbf{q})\cdot\widetilde{\mathbf{Z}}_{e}</annotation></semantics></math>. Deriving from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib87" title="" class="ltx_ref">Alemi et al. (2017)</a></cite>, the lower bound is:</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\geqslant-\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{NCE}}=\log\frac{\exp\big(\operatorname{sim}(\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}},\mathbf{q})/\tau\big)}{\sum_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{B}}\exp\big(\operatorname{sim}(\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}},\mathbf{q}^{\prime})/\tau\big)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⩾</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">NCE</mtext></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">sim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐆</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">sim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐆</mi><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\geqslant-\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{NCE}}=\log\frac{\exp\big(\operatorname{sim}(\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}},\mathbf{q})/\tau\big)}{\sum_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{B}}\exp\big(\operatorname{sim}(\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}},\mathbf{q}^{\prime})/\tau\big)},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}},\mathbf{q}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐆</mi><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}},\mathbf{q}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is the negative sample pair.<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The primary goal is to maximize the mutual information <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure the retrieved subgraph <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> retains sufficient semantic information relevant to the query <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the exact computation involves high-dimensional integration over the joint distribution, we derive a tractable lower bound via variational estimation.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Variational Lower Bound Derivation.<span id="A3.SS3.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
By definition, mutual information is the reduction in uncertainty of <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})=H(\mathbf{q})-H(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})=H(\mathbf{q})-H(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since the entropy of the query distribution <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\mathbf{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\mathbf{q})</annotation></semantics></math> is constant with respect to the subgraph selector, maximizing mutual information is equivalent to minimizing conditional entropy <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
However, the true posterior distribution <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math> is unknown. We introduce a variational distribution <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math> to approximate this posterior. Leveraging the non-negativity of the Kullback-Leibler divergence, <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{Q}(\mathbf{p}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})~||~\mathbb{Q}(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}))\geqslant 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{Q}(\mathbf{p}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})~||~\mathbb{Q}(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}))\geqslant 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we establish the following bound:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\mathbf{q};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{q},\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})}\left[\log\frac{\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})}{\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{q})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{q},\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})}\left[\log\frac{\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})}{\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{q})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{q},\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})}\left[\log\mathbb{Q}(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\right]+\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{P}~||~\mathbb{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>ℚ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{q},\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})}\left[\log\mathbb{Q}(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\right]+\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{P}~||~\mathbb{Q})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{q},\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})}\left[\log\mathbb{Q}(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{q},\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})}\left[\log\mathbb{Q}(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">which implies that maximizing the log-likelihood of the variational distribution is a valid proxy for mutual information.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Modeling Semantic Alignment.<span id="A3.SS3.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
To bridge the gap between the query and the graph structure, we model the variational distribution <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℚ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> using an energy-based formulation. The probability is proportional to the semantic similarity between the pooled subgraph representation <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the query embedding <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})=\frac{\exp(\operatorname{sim}(\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}},\mathbf{q})/\tau)}{\Pi(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})=\frac{\exp(\operatorname{sim}(\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}},\mathbf{q})/\tau)}{\Pi(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is a temperature hyper-parameter and <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the partition function. This formulation effectively encourages aligning the embedding spaces of relevant subgraphs and queries.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tractable NCE Approximation.<span id="A3.SS3.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Directly computing the partition <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math> requires summing over the entire query space, which is computationally infeasible. Following the InfoNCE principle <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib89" title="" class="ltx_ref">Oord et al., 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib88" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2020</a>)</cite>, we approximate this term using a batch of negative samples <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>. The learning problem is thus cast as a discrimination task: identifying the true query <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math> from a set of distractors (negative samples):</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\log\mathbb{Q}(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\right]\doteq\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}\left[\log\frac{\exp(\operatorname{sim}(\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}},\mathbf{q})/\tau)}{\sum_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{B}}\exp(\operatorname{sim}(\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}},\mathbf{q}^{\prime})/\tau)}\right]=-\mathcal{L}_{\text{NCE}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≐</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>NCE</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\log\mathbb{Q}(\mathbf{q}\mid\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\right]\doteq\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}\left[\log\frac{\exp(\operatorname{sim}(\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}},\mathbf{q})/\tau)}{\sum_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{B}}\exp(\operatorname{sim}(\mathbf{G}_{\mathbf{q}^{\prime}},\mathbf{q}^{\prime})/\tau)}\right]=-\mathcal{L}_{\text{NCE}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We conclude the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4. </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Proposition 4.4 (Upper Bound of 𝐼(𝒢,𝒢_q)). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first restate Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Proposition 4.4 (Upper Bound of 𝐼(𝒢,𝒢_q)). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a> for reference.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="150.84" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 150.84" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,150.84) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 146.21 C 0 148.77 2.07 150.84 4.63 150.84 L 472.75 150.84 C 475.3 150.84 477.38 148.77 477.38 146.21 L 477.38 4.63 C 477.38 2.07 475.3 0 472.75 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 146.21 C 0.69 148.39 2.45 150.15 4.63 150.15 L 472.75 150.15 C 474.92 150.15 476.68 148.39 476.68 146.21 L 476.68 4.63 C 476.68 2.45 474.92 0.69 472.75 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.32 101.94)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.73em;--ltx-fo-height:3.15em;--ltx-fo-depth:6.98em;font-size:10pt;" height="140.2" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 43.59)" width="466.73"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.73em;">
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Proposition 4.4 (Upper Bound of 𝐼(𝒢,𝒢_q)). ‣ 4.2. Label-free IB Optimized Subgraph Selector ‣ 4. Proposed Framework: Gfm-Retriever ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> (</span><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Upper Bound of <math id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathcal{G};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">q</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathcal{G};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">)
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Denote the subgraph size and connectivity penalizers as:</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{size}}=\sum\nolimits_{e\in\mathcal{V}}S_{e}(\mathbf{q}),\;\;\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{con}}=\operatorname{Tr}\big(\mathbf{S}_{e}(\mathbf{q})^{\top}\mathbf{L}\mathbf{S}_{e}(\mathbf{q})\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">size</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">con</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐒</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐋𝐒</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{size}}=\sum\nolimits_{e\in\mathcal{V}}S_{e}(\mathbf{q}),\;\;\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{con}}=\operatorname{Tr}\big(\mathbf{S}_{e}(\mathbf{q})^{\top}\mathbf{L}\mathbf{S}_{e}(\mathbf{q})\big),</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{e}(\mathbf{q})\in[\textnormal{0},\textnormal{1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mtext></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{e}(\mathbf{q})\in[\textnormal{0},\textnormal{1}]</annotation></semantics></math> is entity selection probability, <math id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}_{e}(\mathbf{q})\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{V}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐒</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}_{e}(\mathbf{q})\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{V}|}</annotation></semantics></math> is the soft selection vector, <math id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalized graph Laplacian, and <math id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Tr}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Tr}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> calculates the trace of a matrix.
The upper bound is:</span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathcal{G};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\leqslant\beta_{\textnormal{1}}\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{size}}+\beta_{\textnormal{2}}\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{con}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">size</mtext></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">con</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathcal{G};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\leqslant\beta_{\textnormal{1}}\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{size}}+\beta_{\textnormal{2}}\mathcal{L}_{\textnormal{con}},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\textnormal{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\textnormal{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\textnormal{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\textnormal{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> are hyper-parameters.<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">This compression term prevents the subgraph selector from retrieving the entire graph and encourages the identification of a “minimal” subgraph. We prove that minimizing the two proposed structural penalizers is equivalent to minimizing an upper bound of this mutual information.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Variational Upper Bound Derivation.<span id="A3.SS4.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Let <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\mid\mathcal{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\mid\mathcal{G})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the encoding distribution (</span></span><span id="A3.SS4.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span><span id="A3.SS4.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text">, the subgraph selection process). We construct an upper bound by introducing an arbitrary prior distribution <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math> over the space of possible subgraphs:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\mathcal{G};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\mathcal{G};\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G})}\left[\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\mid\mathcal{G})~||~\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G})}\left[\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\mid\mathcal{G})~||~\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G})}\left[\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\mid\mathcal{G})~||~r(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}))\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G})}\left[\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\mid\mathcal{G})~||~r(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}))\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Minimizing KL divergence penalizes the learned subgraph distribution to conform to properties specified by the prior <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gibbs Prior for Graph Structure.<span id="A3.SS4.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
To inject the inductive biases that valid reasoning paths should be dense and connected, we explicitly define the prior <math id="A3.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math> as a Gibbs distribution (or Boltzmann distribution). The energy function <math id="A3.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math> encodes the cost of a subgraph configuration:</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})=\frac{1}{Z}\exp\left(-E(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})=\frac{1}{Z}\exp\left(-E(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.E18.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">where</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})=\beta_{1}E_{\text{size}}+\beta_{2}E_{\text{con}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>size</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>con</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})=\beta_{1}E_{\text{size}}+\beta_{2}E_{\text{con}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">The constant <math id="A3.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> denotes Zustandssumme (German for “sum over states”). Its mathematical definition is the normalized sum of the exponential of the energy over all possible states:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\sum_{\mathcal{G}^{\prime}\in\Omega}\exp(-E(\mathcal{G}^{\prime}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\sum_{\mathcal{G}^{\prime}\in\Omega}\exp(-E(\mathcal{G}^{\prime})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">The specific forms of the energy terms are derived from two priors:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1) Sparsity via Laplace Prior.<span id="A3.SS4.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Assuming the edge selection follows a Laplace distribution centered at zero, its negative log-likelihood corresponds to the <math id="A3.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm of the selection probabilities, yielding <math id="A3.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\text{size}}=\sum S_{e}(\mathbf{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>size</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\text{size}}=\sum S_{e}(\mathbf{q})</annotation></semantics></math>, denoting as <math id="A3.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{size}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>size</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{size}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2) Connectivity via GMRF Prior.<span id="A3.SS4.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Assuming the selection variables follow a Gaussian Markov Random Field (GMRF) over the structure, the energy is defined by the graph Laplacian quadratic form, yielding <math id="A3.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\text{con}}=\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{S}_{e}(\mathbf{q})^{\top}\mathbf{L}\mathbf{S}_{e}(\mathbf{q}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>con</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐋𝐒</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\text{con}}=\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{S}_{e}(\mathbf{q})^{\top}\mathbf{L}\mathbf{S}_{e}(\mathbf{q}))</annotation></semantics></math>, denoting as <math id="A3.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{con}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>con</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{con}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Equivalence to Loss Minimization.<span id="A3.SS4.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
We substitute the Gibbs prior back into the KL divergence term. Note that the entropy of the encoder <math id="A3.SS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\mid\mathcal{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\mid\mathcal{G})</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by the subgraph selector’s confidence. Assuming a deterministic or low-variance selection process, this entropy term can be treated as a constant. The optimization objective simplifies as follows:</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\min\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{P}(\cdot\mid\mathcal{G})~||~r(\cdot))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{P}(\cdot\mid\mathcal{G})~||~r(\cdot))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow\min\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\mid\mathcal{G})}\left[-\log r(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow\min\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\mid\mathcal{G})}\left[-\log r(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow\min\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\mid\mathcal{G})}\left[-\log\left(\frac{1}{Z}\exp(-E(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}))\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow\min\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\mid\mathcal{G})}\left[-\log\left(\frac{1}{Z}\exp(-E(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}))\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow\min\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\mid\mathcal{G})}\left[\beta_{1}\mathcal{L}_{\text{size}}+\beta_{2}\mathcal{L}_{\text{con}}+\log Z\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>size</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>con</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow\min\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{G}_{\mathbf{q}}\mid\mathcal{G})}\left[\beta_{1}\mathcal{L}_{\text{size}}+\beta_{2}\mathcal{L}_{\text{con}}+\log Z\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.20)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow\min\left(\beta_{1}\mathcal{L}_{\text{size}}+\beta_{2}\mathcal{L}_{\text{con}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>size</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>con</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow\min\left(\beta_{1}\mathcal{L}_{\text{size}}+\beta_{2}\mathcal{L}_{\text{con}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">We conclude the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table D.1. </span>Statistics of the general multi-hop QA datasets.</figcaption>
<div id="A4.T1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:258.8pt;height:23.3pt;vertical-align:-10.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-211.3pt,19.1pt) scale(0.379764830958086,0.379764830958086) ;">
<table id="A4.T1.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A4.T1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dataset</span></td>
<td id="A4.T1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\#" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>#</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\#</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A4.T1.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Q-doc Pair</span></td>
<td id="A4.T1.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\#" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>#</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\#</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A4.T1.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Document</span></td>
<td id="A4.T1.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\#" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>#</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\#</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A4.T1.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KG</span></td>
