</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Experiment Details</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide additional experimental details.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1. </span>Datasets Details</h3>

<section id="A4.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.1.1. </span>General Multi-hop QA Datasets</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following prior work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, we conduct experiments on <span id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">three</span> benchmark datasets for the multi-hop question answering task, namely <span id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">HotpotQA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib90" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2018b</a>)</cite>, <span id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MuSiQue</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib91" title="" class="ltx_ref">Trivedi et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, and <span id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">2WikiMultiHopQA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib92" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al., 2020</a>)</cite>.
The statistics are listed in Table <a href="#A4.T1" title="Table D.1 ‣ C.4. Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>. A brief description of each dataset is provided below.</p>
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">HotpotQA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib90" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2018b</a>)</cite>: a large-scale multi-hop question answering dataset comprising 97k examples. Each question is paired with up to two gold supporting documents and several distractors. Answering typically requires combining evidence from both documents, testing the ability to perform fine-grained reasoning.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MuSiQue</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib91" title="" class="ltx_ref">Trivedi et al., 2022</a>)</cite>: contains 25k carefully curated multi-hop questions that require two to four reasoning steps. The questions are constructed to encourage compositional reasoning over multiple documents, making it a challenging benchmark for evaluating multi-step semantic understanding.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">2WikiMultiHopQA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib92" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al., 2020</a>)</cite>: a Wikipedia-based multi-hop QA dataset with 192k questions. Each question is designed to require reasoning over two or four different Wikipedia articles. The dataset highlights diverse reasoning patterns across factual content, providing a comprehensive testbed.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.1.2. </span>Domain-specific QA Datasets</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To assess the generalization ability of <span id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Gfm</span>-Retriever across diverse application scenarios, we further evaluate it on <span id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">seven</span> multi-hop QA benchmarks spanning multiple domains, including: <span id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1) Biomedical:</span> <span id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PubMedQA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib110" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jin et al., 2019</a>)</cite>; <span id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2) Customer Support:</span> <span id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DelucionQA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib111" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sadat et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, <span id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TechQA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib112" title="" class="ltx_ref">Castelli et al., 2020</a>)</cite>, <span id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ExpertQA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib113" title="" class="ltx_ref">Malaviya et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and <span id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">EManual</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib114" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nandy et al., 2021</a>)</cite>; and <span id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(3) General Knowledge:</span> <span id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MS</span> <span id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Marco</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib115" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nguyen et al., 2016</a>)</cite> and <span id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">HAGRID</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib116" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kamalloo et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. The statistics of the datasets are listed in Table <a href="#A4.T2" title="Table D.2 ‣ C.4. Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2. </span>Baseline Details</h3>

