</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.14" class="ltx_p" style="width:294.2pt;"><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:90%;width:294.2pt;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.14.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.14.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:18.9pt;"> </span><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.14.1.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:275.3pt;">
<span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">        "A Kiss for Corliss is a 1949 American comedy film directed by Richard Wallace and written by Howard Dimsdale.",</span>
</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.15" class="ltx_p" style="width:294.2pt;"><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:90%;width:294.2pt;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.15.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.15.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:18.9pt;"> </span><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.15.1.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:275.3pt;">
<span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p15.1" class="ltx_p">        " It stars Shirley Temple in her final starring role as well as her final film appearance.",</span>
</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.16" class="ltx_p" style="width:294.2pt;"><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:90%;width:294.2pt;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.16.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:294.2pt;">
<span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">        ’ It is a sequel to the 1945 film "Kiss and Tell".’,</span>
</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.17" class="ltx_p" style="width:294.2pt;"><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:90%;width:294.2pt;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.17.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.17.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.17.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:18.9pt;"> </span><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.17.1.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:275.3pt;">
<span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p17.1" class="ltx_p">        ’ "A Kiss for Corliss" was retitled "Almost a Bride" before release and this title appears in the title sequence.’,</span>
</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.18" class="ltx_p" style="width:294.2pt;"><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:90%;width:294.2pt;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.18.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.18.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.18.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:18.9pt;"> </span><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.18.1.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:275.3pt;">
<span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p18.1" class="ltx_p">        " The film was released on November 25, 1949, by United Artists.",</span>
</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.19" class="ltx_p" style="width:294.2pt;"><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:90%;width:294.2pt;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="A4.SS3.pic1.p107.19.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:294.2pt;">
