<td id="A5.T1.2.1.28.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">256</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.2.1.29" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.29.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Regularization weight <math id="A5.T1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.29.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.01</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.2.1.30" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.30.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Regularization weight <math id="A5.T1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.30.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.1</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.2.1.31" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.31.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Gumbel-Sigmoid temperature <math id="A5.T1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.31.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.5</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.2.1.32" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.32.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">InfoNCE temperature <math id="A5.T1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.32.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.07</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.2.1.33" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.33.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Optimizer</td>
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.33.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">AdamW</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.2.1.34" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.34.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Learning rate</td>
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.34.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">5e-4</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.2.1.35" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.35.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Batch size</td>
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.35.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">8</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.2.1.36" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.36.1" class="ltx_td"></td>
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.36.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Number of fine-tuning epochs</td>
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.36.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">20</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.2.1.37" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.37.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" rowspan="3"><span id="A5.T1.2.1.37.1.1" class="ltx_text">Inference (QA)</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.37.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Number of top-<math id="A5.T1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> documents</td>
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.37.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">5</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.2.1.38" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.38.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Maximum DFS depth <math id="A5.T1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.38.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">3</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.2.1.39" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.39.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Random seed</td>
<td id="A5.T1.2.1.39.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">1024</td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1. </span>Implementation Details of <span id="A5.SS1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Gfm</span>-Retriever</h3>

<section id="A5.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.1.1. </span>Pre-training Data</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We follow the pre-training data processing pipeline released by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo et al. (2025)</a></cite> to prepare large-scale pre-training data.
Specifically, a total of 60K pre-training instances are sampled from the training splits of <span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">HotpotQA</span>, <span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MuSiQue</span>, and <span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">2WikiMultiHopQA</span>, and merge their associated candidate passages to form the document corpus.
To build KG, the OpenIE-based extraction strategy is adopted, using <span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GPT-4o-mini</span> with prompts described in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib103" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gutiérrez et al. (2024)</a></cite> to extract entities, relations, and triples from the corpus.
Entity resolution is then performed by computing pairwise embedding similarities <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(e_{i},e_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(e_{i},e_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> with <span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ColBERTv2</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib97" title="" class="ltx_ref">Santhanam et al., 2022</a>)</cite>:</p>
<table id="A5.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(E.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(e_{i},e_{j})=\textsc{TextEmb}(e_{i})^{\top}\textsc{TextEmb}(e_{j})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">TextEmb</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">TextEmb</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(e_{i},e_{j})=\textsc{TextEmb}(e_{i})^{\top}\textsc{TextEmb}(e_{j}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where a new equivalence relation <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(e_{i},\equiv,e_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">≡</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(e_{i},\equiv,e_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> is added when their embedding similarity exceeds a threshold <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.8</annotation></semantics></math>.
To control the scale of each index, the sampled data are partitioned into subsets of approximately 1K questions and 10K documents.
This results in 60 knowledge graph indexes paired with corresponding question-document sets, which are used for large-scale pre-training.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.1.2. </span>Model Configurations</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Gfm</span>-Retriever is implemented as a query-conditioned GNN with 6 message-passing layers with a hidden size of 512. Entity and relation embeddings are initialized from the frozen <span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">all-mpnet-v2</span> sentence encoder <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib109" title="" class="ltx_ref">SBERT, 2021</a>)</cite> in 768 dimensions. Each layer performs relation-aware message passing using a bilinear interaction function followed by sum aggregation, while relation states are refined through a lightweight 2-layer MLP to capture context-dependent transformations. The pre-trained <span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Gfm</span>-Retriever contains approximately 8.1M trainable parameters and serves as a generalized and cross-domain retriever that produces query-conditioned entity embeddings for subgraph selection. For document ranking, we return the top-5 document corpus.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.1.3. </span>Hyper-paramters</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide hyper-parameter configurations of pre-training, fine-tuning, and inference stages in Table <a href="#A5.T1" title="Table E.1 ‣ Appendix E Implementation Details ‣ Retrieving Minimal and Sufficient Reasoning Subgraphswith Graph Foundation Models for Path-aware GraphRAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2. </span>Implementation Details of Baselines</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide the baseline methods implementations as follows.</p>
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GPT-4o-mini</span>: <a href="https://platform.openai.com" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://platform.openai.com</a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BM25</span>: <a href="https://github.com/jxmorris12/bm25_pt" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/jxmorris12/bm25_pt</a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Contriever</span>: <a href="https://github.com/facebookresearch/contriever" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/facebookresearch/contriever</a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GTR</span>: <a href="https://github.com/google-research/t5x_retrieval#dense-retrieval-models" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/google-research/t5x_retrieval#dense-retrieval-models</a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ColBERTv2</span>: <a href="https://github.com/stanford-futuredata/ColBERT" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/stanford-futuredata/ColBERT</a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RAPTOR</span>: <a href="https://github.com/parthsarthi03/raptor" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/parthsarthi03/raptor</a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Proposition</span>: <a href="https://github.com/chentong0/factoid-wiki" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/chentong0/factoid-wiki</a>.</p>
